```js
// Assuming `tsLineMap` and `tsWriter` are already defined elsewhere in your script
functions.emitNewLineBeforeLeadingComments({
  lineMap: tsLineMap,          // the line‑map object for the TS file
  writer: tsWriter,            // the writer instance that will modify the file
  node: 42,                    // the numeric position of the target node
  leadingComments: [],         // optional – defaults to an empty array if omitted
});
```

This call tells the helper to look up the line information for the node at position 42, then use the provided `tsWriter` to emit a newline before any leading comments that might be attached to that node. If you don’t need to supply a custom `leadingComments` array, you can simply omit that property; the helper will default it to an empty array.

